# Overview

[Cursor Execution Safety Protocol — Mandatory]

This project requires strict execution safety rules.

1. Command execution must always wait for explicit user approval (Allow).
   - If approval wait exceeds 10 seconds, cancel and restart command.
   - Never continue or chain commands after delayed approval.

2. Single execution rule:
   - One command → finish → output → next step.
   - No parallel, background, chained, or batch commands.

3. Build & test standard:
   - Always run lint → build → test (if exists).
   - If lint does not exist, run build only.

4. Error handling:
   - On first error:
     → stop execution
     → analyze logs
     → apply minimal diff fix
     → re-run single command

5. Output rule:
   - Do NOT truncate logs with head/tail.
   - Show full logs → summarize → fix → re-run.

6. Session recovery:
   - On hanging, stalled, or delayed runs:
     → cancel immediately
     → restart in fresh session
     → never resume mid-process.

7. KR / EN dual maintenance:
   - If KR and EN versions exist, always update both.
   - Maintain identical logic and structure, only text differs.

8. Completion criteria:
   - lint + build (+ test if exists) must pass.
   - Zero type errors.
   - Zero runtime errors.
   - Warnings must be reported.

These rules override any autonomous execution behavior.

